e655d8a54880cf550567dda0e9a1a33f6ee98df5 2023-03-09 01:14:03 +0100 [libc++] Granularize __mutex_base
1641a7c1cb198cb5bb4b96d0890d1e7d13e089c4 2014-03-26 02:45:04 +0000 Implement LWG issue #2135. If something goes wrong in condition_variable::wait, call terminate() rather than throwing an error. Do this indirectly, by marking the call as 'noexcept'. This is better than just calling terminate() directly, because it gives a better error message on the console.
80232d036bac5e417cf28ab597802863eae05e96 2014-03-26 02:45:04 +0000 Implement LWG issue #2135. If something goes wrong in condition_variable::wait, call terminate() rather than throwing an error. Do this indirectly, by marking the call as 'noexcept'. This is better than just calling terminate() directly, because it gives a better error message on the console.
